<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wars of Kappel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1529–1531</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Kappel Wars, Second War of Kappel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wars of Kappel were two religious wars between Reformed Zürich and the Catholic cantons of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>. The first, in 1529, ended without battle in the First Peace of Kappel. In the second, on 11 October 1531, the Catholic forces defeated Zürich at Kappel am <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albi">Albis</a>, killing the reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huldrych-zwingli">Huldrych Zwingli</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-peace-of-kappel">Second Peace of Kappel</a> let each canton decide its own religion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wars-of-kappel.jpg" alt="Wars of Kappel" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Stumpf · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_battle_of_Kappel_1531_(88362511).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
